menu "Attadipa firmware"

choice ATTADIPA_BOARD
    prompt "Board this image is composed for"
    default ATTADIPA_BOARD_WAVESHARE_AMOLED_206
    help
        main/ is the composition root (CMakeLists.txt): the one place that
        may know which board answers, so this is where it is chosen.
        Everything above it asks the board profile what the device can do.

config ATTADIPA_BOARD_WAVESHARE_AMOLED_206
    bool "Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-2.06"

config ATTADIPA_BOARD_TWATCH_S3_PLUS
    bool "LilyGO T-Watch S3 Plus (bring-up: panel, touch, rails)"
    help
        First slice (#417): ST7789 panel, FT6336U touch and ALDO2/ALDO3.
        No RTC, NVS, physical input or sleep yet. Stack sdkconfig.twatch on
        sdkconfig.defaults; it also sets the flash mode the factory image
        uses.

endchoice

config ATTADIPA_TWATCH_PANEL_RESET_EXTRA_MS
    int "Extra wait after the ST7789 software reset, ms"
    depends on ATTADIPA_BOARD_TWATCH_S3_PLUS
    default 100
    range 0 1000
    help
        ESP-IDF waits 20 ms after SWRESET; the ST7789V3 datasheet asks for
        120 ms before SLPOUT from sleep-in. 100 is arm C of the experiment
        in docs/research/TWATCH_S3_PLUS_BSP_REUSE.md section 11; 0 is arm
        A, the driver as shipped.

config ATTADIPA_TWATCH_PANEL_INVERT
    bool "Invert the panel's colours (INVON), as the vendor does"
    depends on ATTADIPA_BOARD_TWATCH_S3_PLUS
    default y
    help
        SWRESET leaves the ST7789 with inversion off. LilyGoLib sends INVON
        (21h) through the panel API rather than from its command table
        (TWATCH_S3_PLUS_BSP_REUSE.md section 5), so arm B does not carry it
        and it has to be a choice of its own. Whether this panel wants it is
        what the section 11 swatch photographs: inverted, red reads cyan
        and the white block black.

config ATTADIPA_TWATCH_PANEL_VENDOR_TABLE
    bool "Send LilyGO's panel command table after init (arm B)"
    depends on ATTADIPA_BOARD_TWATCH_S3_PLUS
    default n
    help
        The MIT-licensed table transcribed in TWATCH_S3_PLUS_BSP_REUSE.md
        section 5, sent as data over esp_lcd_panel_io_tx_param(). Only if
        arm C shows nothing; whether it is needed is UNKNOWN until the
        photograph.

config ATTADIPA_WATCH_CONTROL
    bool "USB watch-control endpoint"
    # The endpoint is wired through the Waveshare backend and physical_input;
    # the T-Watch slice has neither yet, so the choice is refused rather than
    # failing at the link.
    depends on ATTADIPA_BOARD_WAVESHARE_AMOLED_206
    default n
    # The screenshot opcode calls lv_snapshot_take_to_draw_buf(), which LVGL
    # compiles out under LV_USE_SNAPSHOT=n -- and n is its own default. Without
    # this line the two symbols that must move together lived in two files with
    # nothing joining them, and turning the endpoint on the obvious way (this
    # menu, then a build) failed at the link rather than at the choice.
    select LV_USE_SNAPSHOT
    help
        Enable the debug control plane over USB-Serial/JTAG: screenshots,
        remote input, and the time and mesh provisioning opcodes. Any host
        that can open the port can use all of it; there is no
        authentication, so this is a bench image rather than a product one.
        Physical touch and the case buttons are NOT gated by this symbol --
        they live in physical_input.cpp and are in every image (#346).
        The feature owns one full RGB565 frame in PSRAM while running, and
        selects LV_USE_SNAPSHOT, which its screenshot opcode needs.

config ATTADIPA_I2C_PROBE
    bool "I2C bring-up probe"
    default n
    help
        Scan the I2C bus on the pins below and log every address that
        acknowledges, then read the AXP2101 charge-voltage register if one
        answered. A bring-up instrument for a board this firmware has no
        driver for; it writes no register and asserts no board identity.

config ATTADIPA_I2C_PROBE_SDA
    int "I2C probe SDA GPIO"
    depends on ATTADIPA_I2C_PROBE
    default 10

config ATTADIPA_I2C_PROBE_SCL
    int "I2C probe SCL GPIO"
    depends on ATTADIPA_I2C_PROBE
    default 11

endmenu
